-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Voyager ML pipeline (Bioqore): seed sweeps and decision agreement
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:
  - github.com/Bioqore/voyager-ml-pipeline (commit 4649115, 2026-08-05)
    ensemble_method/ensemble_ml_libraries/seed_sweep.py (run_seed_sweep,
    compute_decision_stability, compute_per_sample_variance: rerun the whole
    pipeline with N seeds and report, per sample, how many seeds agree on the
    decision, plus an overall agreement rate), and
    ensemble_method/ensemble_ml_libraries/driver_analysis_and_interpretability/
    drivers.py (Spearman drivers with bootstrap summaries).

Authors (from the repository's history): Tim (timbioqore, tlorgeree),
Kai Suematsu (ks-bio).

Permission: the owner of the repository authorized taking its ideas and code
into Kalos on 2026-11-20 ("take everything"). The repository carries no license
file; it is used here under that permission.

What was adapted (idea credit; re-implemented, no source file copied):
  - the seed sweep with per-item agreement and an overall agreement rate,
    re-implemented for batch proposals as the opt-in proposal stability check:
    kalos/core/stability.py and kalos/portal/analysis_parts/stability.py
    (agreement = the fraction of rerun seeds whose batch contains a recipe
    within the optimizer's near-duplicate tolerance; served batch unchanged);
  - a second reading of the drivers next to the Spearman panel, here as GP
    relevance with a recipe-subsample interval and a collinearity check:
    kalos/core/gp_relevance.py, kalos/core/collinearity.py and
    kalos/portal/analysis_parts/driver_opinion.py.
Kalos's own Spearman driver panel (kalos/core/drivers.py) predates this port.
